@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# 9. Persist due times before exposing them
+
+Status: Accepted
+
+Response promises must survive priority and configuration changes. Each ticket stores an additive ISO `due` field,
+computed once from creation and configured priority hours. Startup fills only missing values and saves atomically before
+listening; creation writes due even when presentation is disabled. DUE_TIMES=on gates ticket presentation and overdue
+query handling. Backfill leaves business audit and notifications unchanged.
+
+The envelope remains version 1 so 1.4.0 can read every ticket after rollback. Its writer discards unknown due fields,
+so operators must preserve due values separately if returning to the new release after rollback writes.
